## Future Workflow

### Bumping to a new version `5.3.0`
```bash
bun run docs:bump 5.2.0 5.3.0
```
This will:
1. Copy `content/api/5.2.0/` → `content/api/5.3.0/`
2. Run `git subtree split` to create `release/5.2.0` branch
3. Add `5.2.0` as a git submodule
4. Run [sync-versions.ts](file:///d:/_Projects/06_PSJ-Docs/psjnext/apps/docs/scripts/sync-versions.ts) → auto-updates all 3 files

### Manual sync (e.g. after checking out a branch)
```bash
bun run sync-versions
```

### Preview without writing
```bash
bun run sync-versions --dry-run
```

> [!NOTE]
> `predev` and `prebuild` hooks run [sync-versions.ts](file:///d:/_Projects/06_PSJ-Docs/psjnext/apps/docs/scripts/sync-versions.ts) automatically before every `next dev` / `next build`.
